---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About & License · NexFilm Engine" lang="en">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-16">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-accent block mb-2">About & Philosophy</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">About NexFilm Engine</h1>
      <p class="text-text-secondary text-base mt-4">
        A transparent, physically grounded desktop workspace dedicated to analog film digitization.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-12">
      <!-- Mission -->
      <section class="p-8 rounded-2xl border border-darkroom-line bg-darkroom-panel space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Origins & Vision</h2>
        <div class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed space-y-3">
          <p>
            For years, the film negative conversion ecosystem has been dominated by costly closed-source plugins and black-box neural presets. Such solutions often guess colors through arbitrary tone curves, leading to wild inconsistencies across varied exposures and copy stands.
          </p>
          <p>
            NexFilm Engine was created to anchor negative conversion back into physical reality: unexposed film base subtraction, logarithmic optical transmission physics, and roll-wide white point calibration that keeps an entire roll cohesive.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Tech Stack -->
      <section class="p-8 rounded-2xl border border-darkroom-line bg-darkroom-panel space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Technology & Architecture</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-darkroom-canvas border border-darkroom-line">
            <span class="font-mono text-accent font-bold">Rust + Tauri 2:</span>
            <p class="text-text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Blazing native performance with lightweight memory footprints, bypassing heavyweight Electron bundles.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-darkroom-canvas border border-darkroom-line">
            <span class="font-mono text-emerald-400 font-bold">WebGL 2.0 Shaders:</span>
            <p class="text-text-muted mt-1 text-xs">GPU-accelerated pipeline providing fluid 60FPS real-time color grading and curve feedback.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-darkroom-canvas border border-darkroom-line">
            <span class="font-mono text-amber-400 font-bold">Local SQLite Database:</span>
            <p class="text-text-muted mt-1 text-xs">All edit parameters, roll notes, and thumbnails persist locally without any telemetry or cloud dependencies.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-darkroom-canvas border border-darkroom-line">
            <span class="font-mono text-purple-400 font-bold">LibRaw Native Decoder:</span>
            <p class="text-text-muted mt-1 text-xs">Cross-platform decoding for camera RAWs and gigabyte-scale Imacon/Flextight scanner formats.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Credits -->
      <section class="p-8 rounded-2xl border border-darkroom-line bg-darkroom-panel space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Theoretical Credits</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
          Special thanks to researchers <code class="text-accent font-mono">@黄昊Haosky</code> and <code class="text-accent font-mono">@V777</code> on Zhihu for openly sharing foundational insights into scientific orange-mask removal, logarithmic optical density calculations, and analog color science.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- License -->
      <section class="p-8 rounded-2xl border border-darkroom-line bg-darkroom-panel space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Open Source License (GPL-3.0)</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
          NexFilm Engine is licensed under the <strong class="text-white">GNU General Public License v3.0</strong>. You are free to run, inspect, modify, and distribute the software, provided all derivative works remain open source under the same license terms.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <a 
            href="https://github.com/BillyDu-TJ/NexFilm/blob/main/LICENSE" 
            target="_blank" 
            class="text-xs font-mono text-accent hover:underline"
          >
            Read the full GNU General Public License v3.0 →
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
